                              -=-
                     -=-  Stock Market -=-
                              -=-

    An online game where you compete against 24 of your fellow users.
The object is to become the first investor to increase your net worth to
$1,000,000 or more.

    All seats are available on a first come, first serve basis.
Investors will start with $50,000.  You must visit the Stock Market at
least once every 10 days or your seat will be sold to make room for other
investors.  Any investor that owns no stock and whose cash holdings fall
below $100 will also have his seat sold.


   There are 9 options available in the Stock Market.  They are:

                [1] The Big Board
                [2] Your Portfolio
                [3] List of Investors and their Net Worth
                [4] Check a Company and its Stockholder
                [5] Vist your Broker (Buy/Sell Stocks)
                [6] Help and Instructions
                [7] Update Stock Market Prices
                [8] Read Stock Market News
                [X] Exit the Stock Market to The BBS


THE BIG BOARD:  From here, you can view all the different companies that
area available.  Also listed are the current number of shares available
and the price per share.  These prices may change whenever an update is
done.  Listed at the bottom are the volume traded and the price index.
The volume traded is the number of shares that have been bought or sold
today.  The price index is the net change of all companies listed for sale.
Both variables show the current days stats and are reset after midnight.

YOUR PORTFOLIO:  This is where you may view a breakdown of your
individual investments.  You will see all stocks owned, the number of
shares owned and the amount of cash you have available.  Listed next to
shares owned is the net change for that company since scheduled upkeep.
If at any time your cash falls below $-1500 you MUST sell off enough
assets to satisfy the debt or your seat will be sold when you leave.

LIST INVESTORS/NET WORTH:  This is a list of ALL investors and their
current Net Worth.  All players are listed in the order in which they
were admitted to the Stock Market.

CHECK A COMPANY/SHAREHOLDER:  This option allows you to view each
individual company and see who has invested in it as well as how many
shares they own.  Listed across the bottom is the net change in price of
that company's stock.

VISIT YOUR BROKER:  At this option, you may buy and sell your stocks.
Please note there is a 5% Brokerage Fee for all transactions.  Five
shares is the minimum amount that may be transfered when buying or selling,
up to the maxium available.  You may only invest in 7 different companies,
at which time you must sell all of one before you would be able to buy
another.  But you may add to the number of SHARES at any time, regardless of
how many companies you own.

UPDATE STOCK PRICES:  You may do only ONE update per call.  An update will
automatically bring the Big Board to current status, adjusting prices
accordingly.  All dividends (if any), will be paid to ALL stockholders of
that company regardless of who does the update.  Any player that leaves
the Stock Market without doing an update will have it done automatically.

STOCK MARKET NEWS:  The news option will show you any major events that
have taken place in the last two days.  Any dividends that are paid get
recorded here, along with any player that lost their seats, and when a new
game is started.


                               - = -

    While that covers all the menu options, from time to time you will
also see various NOTICES.  Some are beneficial while others may cost you
money.

